  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4a2b061e491659d4e8424ca22aacc1c7, type: 3}
  m_Name: Read_ZoneProfile_Navigation_Mid
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Hecton8.World.WorldExpeditionLoopProfile
  profileId: loop.profile.navigation.mid
  profileLabel: Navigation Mid Read
  entryBeat: Distinct silhouettes and branching space make orientation the main value.
  routineBeat: The player quickly understands that mental mapping matters more than
    raw loot here.
  reliefBeat: Short calm ledges or readable pockets help reset direction.
  pressureBeat: Pressure comes from getting turned around, not from being shoved
    down one line.
  payoffBeat: The reward is better world memory, cleaner returns, and confidence
    in branch choice.
  exitBeat: Leaving should feel easier because the player now owns more of the map
    in their head.
  playerFreedomRule: The player is free to test branches, retreat, or cross-cut between
    landmarks.
  softProgressionPull: The area nudges exploration through readability and curiosity,
    not compulsion.
  optionalDetourRule: Wrong turns should still teach the space and occasionally pay
    out.
  returnLogic: Repeat visits should become smoother as landmark memory grows.
  masteryLogic: Mastery means building your own internal map and faster cross-links.
  playerPromise: Readable branching water that turns confusion into ownership over
    time.
  routeMemoryRule: Memory should come from silhouettes, branch logic, and safe reorientation
    pockets.
  failureMode: If every branch feels the same, the zone loses identity.
